# ─── 3D Photorealistic Tiles: pick ONE of the two below ───────
#
# Both routes render the same Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles. They differ only
# in who bills you and what a leaked credential costs. Anything in a VITE_ var
# is compiled into the public JavaScript bundle and is readable by anyone, so
# assume whichever you choose WILL be seen.
#
# RECOMMENDED: Cesium ion (below). Leave VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY empty.
#   Free Community tier: 1,000 root tiles/month + 15 GB streaming, personal and
#   non-commercial use. When the quota runs out the tiles simply stop and the
#   app falls back to OpenStreetMap. You are never billed.
#   Lock the token down at https://ion.cesium.com/tokens :
#     - scope:     assets:read  (nothing more)
#     - assetIds:  2275207      (Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles only)
#     - allowedUrls: your domain, e.g. https://worldview.khoa.to
#   If it leaks, revoke and reissue in one click. Nothing else is exposed.
VITE_CESIUM_ION_TOKEN=

# ALTERNATIVE: bill Google directly. Only do this if you actually want to pay
# for volume beyond the ion free tier. This key is PUBLIC in the bundle and is
# attached to an uncapped Google Cloud billing account, so if you use it you
# MUST, in https://console.cloud.google.com/google/maps-apis :
#     - restrict the key to the "Map Tiles API" only
#     - add an HTTP referrer restriction for your domain
#     - set a daily quota cap so abuse cannot run up an open-ended bill
# Leave this empty to use the safer ion route above.
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# ─── CCTV Camera Sources ─────────────────────────────────────
# Windy webcam API (reserved, not yet active)
# Get yours: https://api.windy.com/
WINDY_API_KEY=

# Transport for NSW Open Data API
# Register: https://opendata.transport.nsw.gov.au/ → "My Applications" → Create App
NSW_TRANSPORT_API_KEY=

# AISStream.io — Real-time ship/vessel AIS tracking (WebSocket)
# Get yours: https://aisstream.io/ → Register → API Keys
AISSTREAM_API_KEY=
